# Repository file and artifact policy

Read this file before creating, moving, or generating files in this repository.
Paths below are relative to the repository root. This policy applies to all agents
and contributors. Preserve existing work and use the established locations.

## Maintained files: included in Git

| Content | Location |
| --- | --- |
| Application composition and desktop shell | `src/app/` |
| Feature code and focused tests | `src/features/<feature>/` |
| Shared components, utilities, and translation catalogs | `src/shared/` |
| Platform bridges | `src/platform/` |
| Provider adapters and integration contracts | `src/integrations/` |
| Host runtime and its tests | `host/` |
| Expo mobile routes, feature code, shared UI, tests and package tooling | `mobile/` |
| Native application and Tauri configuration | `src-tauri/` |
| Browser scenarios, fixtures, servers, and fixture configurations | `tests/browser/` |
| Assets required by the product | `public/`; branding in `public/brand/` |
| Vendored dependencies and their license notices | `vendor/` |
| Platform build helpers | `scripts/build/` |
| Environment setup helpers | `scripts/setup/` |
| Version and release maintenance | `scripts/release/` |
| Repository and transport checks | `scripts/checks/` |
| Translation maintenance | `scripts/i18n/` |
| Local update implementation, configuration, and tests | `scripts/local-update/` |
| Public local update commands | `scripts/update-local.ps1`, `scripts/update-local.sh` |
| Project skills and feature cards | `.agents/skills/` |
| User guides | `docs/guides/` |
| Integration and host workflow guides | `docs/integrations/` |
| Architecture and maintenance references | `docs/reference/` |
| Shared local update guide | `docs/local-update.md` |
| Issue/PR templates and CI | `.github/` |

Keep unit tests beside their source modules when that is the existing convention.
Place a reusable helper in its maintained script group; place a one-time helper
under `temp/local/<task-id>/`. Required product assets must not depend on `temp/`.
Write maintained documentation in English. Translation catalogs keep their target
languages. Preserve third-party license notices and attribution.

Keep tool entry points and manifests in the root when their tools expect them
there: package/Cargo manifests and locks, TypeScript/Vite/Vitest/Playwright
configuration, HTML application entry points, README, contributing/security/license
files, `AGENTS.md`, and this policy. Do not move these solely to reduce root entries.
Do not introduce another top-level folder or alternate script/document hierarchy
without a concrete need and an update to this policy.

## Agent outputs: local and excluded from Git

The entire `temp/` directory is ignored. Use these locations instead of scattering
development records through the source tree:

| Output | Location |
| --- | --- |
| Task plans, TODOs, research, one-time scripts, and scratch data | `temp/local/<task-id>/` |
| Check logs, benchmark results, screenshots, and visual reviews | `temp/verification/<task-id>/` |
| Temporary builds and browser fixture bundles | `temp/build/<task-id>/` |
| Browser test traces and results | `temp/test-results/<suite>/` |
| Useful retired files kept for later reference | `temp/archive/<original-relative-path>` |
| Git bundles, ref inventories, and history recovery records | `temp/history/` |

Use a short descriptive task ID, for example `2026-10-09-provider-settings`.
Keep one task's outputs together. When retaining useful material, include a short
README describing its purpose, origin, reuse limitations, and any recovery steps.
Do not overwrite another task's outputs or an existing archive entry. Use a versioned
subfolder if the same original path needs another archived version.

Do not create new `.scratch*`, `output/`, `docs/evidence/`, `docs/benchmarks/`,
or dated development-plan/TODO/report files in maintained documentation folders.
Their legacy ignore rules protect old checkouts; they are not approved destinations.
Agent logs and generated captures are not product assets just because they are images.

Keep dependency caches, Cargo targets, and operational build/release packages in
the locations required by their tools and the local update coordinator. Do not move
active packages, databases, credentials, live lock files, or rollback material into
`temp/` as a cleanup shortcut. Credentials remain in the existing credential stores;
never copy them into tracked source or an archive. Preserve useful local material
when cleaning up; do not delete it without task authorization.

## Creating or relocating a file

1. Decide whether the file is maintained product source/documentation or a local
   task output, then select the matching location above.
2. Reuse an existing directory and naming convention. Avoid parallel copies,
   unreferenced asset variants, and root-level experiment files.
3. If moving maintained files, update imports, root/path calculations, package
   commands, CI references, documentation links, and tests in the same change.
   Preserve the public local update entry points and persistent caches.
4. Verify relevant checks and review the Git diff. Check that local outputs are
   ignored with `git check-ignore <path>`; never bypass that with `git add -f`.
5. Run `node scripts/checks/check-repository-hygiene.mjs` before committing.
   Stage only intended paths. PRs still require passing relevant tests and required
   CI checks before merging; this policy does not relax those requirements.

## Organization recorded on 2026-10-09

- Grouped maintained scripts by build, setup, release, checks, translation, and
  local update responsibilities; preserved the public update wrappers.
- Grouped product documentation into guides, integrations, and references while
  preserving the shared local update guide's entry path.
- Moved browser fixture configuration beside the browser tests and redirected
  fixture builds/results into ignored `temp/` locations.
- Retained 99 recoverable historical documents, scripts, assets, and output files
  under `temp/archive/`; preserved history recovery bundles under `temp/history/`.
  Files previously deleted without a Git record or backup could not be recovered.
- Started maintained history with a single consolidated first commit by the
  maintainer. Kept original license notices and explicit MonoCode v0.6 attribution
  and thanks in the project documentation.

This records file organization, not a claim that every test or installed runtime
has passed. Detailed run results belong in `temp/verification/`, not this policy.
Update this file when an approved change adds or changes a maintained file category.
